tician",1938,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197278,"Archer on Horseback",1941,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197279,"The Plucked Goose",1941,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197280,"The Forge of Vulcan and Self-Portrait",1949,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197281,"Hippolytus and His Horse",1959,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197282,"Solitary Horse",1960,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197283,"Mediterranean Friends",1970,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197284,"Sun on the Easel",1973,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197285,"Silent Dialogue",1973,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null],[140197286,"Self-Portrait in Front of the Easel",1975,0,0,null,0,null,null,null,0,0,null]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaries":{"1154410":["The Song of Love is a 1914 painting by Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico. It is one of the most famous works by Chirico and an early example of his pre-surrealist style, though it was painted ten years before the movement was \"founded\" by André Breton in 1924.","The Song of Love"],"3793980":["The Prodigal Son is a painting by the Greek-born Italian artist Giorgio de Chirico.","The Prodigal Son (Giorgio de Chirico)"],"3798257":["The Nostalgia of the Infinite is a painting by Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico, dated of 1911, but most likely painted in 1912–13.","The Nostalgia of the Infinite"],"4091828":["The Great Tower is an oil on canvas painting by the Italian artist Giorgio de Chirico, from 1921. It is held in the Pushkin Museum, in Moscow.","The Great Tower"],"4289293":["Mystery and Melancholy of a Street is a 1914 oil-on-canvas painting by the Italian artist Giorgio de Chirico. It is held in a private collection.","Mystery and Melancholy of a Street"],"5522671":["Gare Montparnasse (The Melancholy of Departure) (Italian: La stazione di Montparnasse) is an oil on canvas painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico, from 1914. It is held at the Museum of Modern Art, in New York.","Gare Montparnasse (The Melancholy of Departure)"],"6507642":["The Transformed Dream is an oil on canvas painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico, from 1913. It is held at the Saint Louis Art Museum, in St. Louis.","The Transformed Dream"],"6823130":["Metaphysical Interior with Biscuits is a 1916 painting by Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico. It is one of the earliest editions in a series of works that extended late into Chirico's career.","Metaphysical Interior with Biscuits"],"7730357":["The Disquieting Muses is a painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico. There are two versions of this painting, the original is in the Gianni Mattioli private collection, in Milan, and the other is at the Pinakothek der Moderne, in Munich.","The Disquieting Muses"],"7732268":["The Enigma of the Hour is an oil on canvas painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico. He created the work during his early period, in Florence, when he focused on metaphysical depictions of town squares and other urban environments.","The Enigma of the Hour"],"7750928":["The Melancholy of Departure is an oil on canvas painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico, from 1916. This painting was created after Chirico returned to Italy from Paris to join the Italian Army in World War I. It is held at the Tate Modern, in London.","The Melancholy of Departure"],"16941559":["Metaphysical Interior with Large Factory is an oil-on-canvas painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico, from 1916. It is part of a series that extended late into de Chirico's career.","Metaphysical Interior with Large Factory"],"16987108":["The Child's Brain is an oil-on-canvas painting by the Italian artist Giorgio de Chirico. It was completed in 1914 in Italy and is an example of the metaphysical art style.","The Child's Brain"],"19918956":["Ariadne is an oil and graphite on canvas 1913 painting by Italian painter Giorgio de Chirico, from 1913. It is held at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, in New York.","Ariadne (Giorgio de Chirico)"],"20816277":["The Soothsayer's Recompense is a 1913 painting by Italian painter Giorgio de Chirico. It is now in the Philadelphia Museum of Art as part of the permanent collection.","The Soothsayer's Recompense"],"24569627":["Venice, Bridge of Rialto is an oil on canvas painting by Giorgio of Chirico, from 1950. It is held at the Museo Soumaya, in Mexico City.","Venice, Bridge of Rialto (Giorgio de Chirico)"],"25449372":["The Double Dream of Spring is a painting by the Italian metaphysical painter Giorgio de Chirico. It is held at the Museum of Modern Art, in New York.","The Double Dream of Spring"],"60415241":["Portrait of Paul Guillaume is a 1915 oil on canvas painting by Giorgio de Chirico of the art dealer Paul Guillaume, now in the Museum of Grenoble, to which it was given by the artist in 1935, inspired by Guillaume's gift of Les époux to the same museum in 1927.","Portrait of Paul Guillaume (De Chirico, Grenoble)"]}}